# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Netlify (and netlify.toml) are fully
# retired — this is the only copy now.
#
# No rules blocking /backend/*, /platform/*, /docs/*, /.github/*, /.git/*
# or /render.yaml: an earlier version had these rewriting to /404.html
# with a 200 status (the only way Cloudflare's _redirects can express
# "not found" — it rejects a literal 404 status outright: "Valid status
# codes are 200, 301, 302, 303, 307, or 308. Got 404."). That 200-status
# rewrite is a real regression from doing nothing: it turns a clean 404
# into a "soft 404" (a real page, real 200, that search engines penalize
# for looking like duplicate/thin content) for paths that were never
# reachable in the first place — build-cf-pages.mjs never uploads
# backend/, platform/, docs/ or .github/ as deployable assets, so these
# paths already 404 correctly with zero rules for them. Confirmed live
# against the real deployment: a path with no matching rule and no
# uploaded file returns a genuine 404, not the soft one these rules used
# to produce.

/find-talent.html  /for-employers.html#categories  301
